, "nodeType": "hadith", "sourceLabel": "Hadith VI", "sourceIdentifier": "VI", "title": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}], "blocks": [{"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "we have been cautioned again and again by the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) and we do believe that he was really the true Messenger of Allah, yet we heed not the caution and go on missing salaat one after the other.", "rawOcrText": "Part I on Discard of Salaat 37 we have been cautioned again and again by the Prophet (Sallalaho alaihe wasallam) and we do believe that he was really the true Messenger of •Allah, yet we heed not the caution and go on missing salaat one after the other. Hadith V Ibn Abbas (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"A person who combines two salaats without any strong excuse reaches one of the doors of kabaa''ir (major sins).\" Hadhrat Ali (Radhiyallaho anho) reports that the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) once said, \"Do not delay in -three things: salaat when its time has set in, burial when the bier is ready and marriage of a solitary woman when her match is found.\" Many personS who consider themselves as practical Muslims perform a -number of their salaats in combination on returning home, on .the very feeble excuses of travel, &ade or occupation. To put salaat off till after its set time without C strong excuse (illness, etc) is a major sin. Although it is not so disastrous as neg- lecting salaat, yet it is quite serious. Hadith VI Abdullah bin Amr (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that once the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) while talking about salaat said: \"For its votary, salaat shall on the Day of Judgement, be a light for him, an argument in his favour, and a means of his deliverance. Whereas there will be no light, no defence and no deliverance", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith V", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ مَنْ جَمَعَ بَيْنَ الصَّلَاتَيْنِ مِنْ غَيْرِ عُذْرٍ فَقَدْ أَتَى بَابًا مِنْ أَبْوَابِ الْكَبَائِرِ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "رواه الحاكم", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Ibn Abbas (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"A person who combines two salaats without any strong excuse reaches one of the doors of kabaa''ir (major sins).\" Hadhrat Ali (Radhiyallaho anho) reports that the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) once said, \"Do not delay in three things: salaat when its time has set in, burial when the bier is ready and marriage of a solitary woman when her match is found.\" Many persons who consider themselves as practical Muslims perform a number of their salaats in combination on returning home, on the very feeble excuses of travel, trade or occupation. To put salaat off till after its set time without a strong excuse (illness, etc) is a major sin. Although it is not so disastrous as neglecting salaat, yet it is quite serious.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith VI", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ ذَكَرَ الصَّلَاةَ يَوْمًا فَقَالَ مَنْ حَافَظَ عَلَيْهَا كَانَتْ لَهُ نُورًا وَبُرْهَانًا وَنَجَاةً يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَمَنْ لَمْ يُحَافِظْ عَلَيْهَا لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ نُورٌ وَلَا بُرْهَانٌ وَلَا نَجَاةٌ وَكَانَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مَعَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامَانَ وَقَارُونَ وَأُبَيِّ بْنِ خَلَفٍ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 7, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "أخرجه أحمد وابن حبان", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "sequenceIndex": 8, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Abdullah bin Amr (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that once the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) while talking about salaat said: \"For its votary, salaat shall on the Day of Judgement, be a light for him, 